    ferieSideSatser:'Holiday pay rates',
    ferieSideWhat:'What is holiday pay?',
    ferieSideWhatBody:'Holiday pay is statutory under the Holiday Act (Ferieloven) § 10. The employer cannot give less than 10,2 %, but collective agreements may give more (typically 12 % for 5 weeks\' holiday). It is normally paid out in June the year after it is earned and is taxable income, even though no tax is withheld at the time of payment.',
    kalkDekningsbidragSideWhat:'What is contribution margin?',
    kalkDekningsbidragSideWhatBody:'CM is price minus variable cost per unit. If you sell for 100 kr and the item costs you 60 kr, the CM is 40 kr.',
    likvidSideWhat:'What is a liquidity budget?',
    likvidSideWhatBody:'The money going in and out of your account, month by month. It is not the same as the profit in the accounts. You see early on whether you need a buffer.',
    bvlSideWhat:'Not included in the figures',
    bvlSideWhatBody:'Document duty and estate agent fees are not included. On a freehold home costing 4 million, the document duty alone is 100 000 kr. If you move within a few years, that can reverse the answer.',
