    kontoAfAktivt: '<strong>Actively managed fund</strong> — the fund manager picks shares manually. Higher fees (1–2%) that eat into returns.',
    kontoAfIndeks: '<strong>Index fund</strong> — passively tracks an entire exchange (e.g. Oslo Stock Exchange or the world). Low fees (0.2–0.4%), and most often beats active funds over time.',
    kontoAfIntro: 'A <strong>fund</strong> is a shared pot that a manager invests on behalf of many savers. You own units in the pot. An <strong>equity fund</strong> invests only in shares, so the risk is spread across many companies. There are two main types:',
    kontoAskBody: '<strong>Share Savings Account (ASK)</strong> is an account type where you can buy and sell shares and equity funds <em>without</em> paying tax on gains until you take the money out of the account. Move freely between funds inside ASK without triggering tax — perfect for long-term share saving.',
    kontoCmpR1A: 'When you withdraw the gain',
    kontoCmpR1L: 'Tax on gains',
    kontoCmpR1V: 'Every time you sell at a gain',
    kontoCmpR2A: 'Tax-free inside the account',
    kontoCmpR2L: 'Switching between funds',
    kontoCmpR2V: 'Triggers tax',
    kontoCmpR3A: 'Shares and equity funds (EEA)',
    kontoCmpR3L: 'What you can buy',
    kontoCmpR3V: 'All funds (also bond funds)',
    kontoCmpR4A: '37.84% on gains',
    kontoCmpR4L: 'Tax on withdrawal',
    kontoCmpR4V: 'None – the tax was paid when you sold',
    kontoCmpThAsk: 'ASK',
    kontoCmpThEgenskap: 'Feature',
    kontoCmpThVanlig: 'Ordinary fund account',
    kontoCtaDesc: 'See what monthly fund saving gives over 10–30 years with compound interest',
    kontoCtaTitle: 'Run the numbers in the savings calculator',
    kontoEyebrowAf: 'Two main types',
    kontoEyebrowAsk: 'Tax-smart account',
    kontoEyebrowCmp: 'Comparison',
    kontoEyebrowVelg: 'Pick an account',
    kontoFbAskBody: 'You can buy, sell and switch shares and equity funds without paying tax on the gain while the money stays in the account. Tax on the gain only falls due when you take it out. Suits long-term share saving.',
    kontoFbAskTitle: 'Share Savings Account (ASK)',
    kontoFbIpsBody: 'Locked until age 62. You get a tax deduction on up to 25 000 kr per year (22% = 5 500 kr saved). Tax is paid only on withdrawal as pension. Suits you if you want extra retirement saving and can lock the money away.',
    kontoFbIpsTitle: 'Individual Pension Saving (IPS)',
    kontoFbTommelBody: 'For long-term saving in shares or equity funds — use <strong>ASK</strong>. It\'s free to open with your bank.',
    kontoFbTommelTitle: 'Rule of thumb',
    kontoFbVanligBody: 'You pay tax on the gain every time you sell, even when you only switch funds. Dividends are taxed in the year you receive them. Suits what can\'t be held in an ASK, such as bond funds.',
    kontoFbVanligTitle: 'Ordinary fund account',
    kontoFootNote: '* 2026 rates. Rules may change — check skatteetaten.no and your fund provider.',
