    regnskapKontoplanK8Lead: 'Financial income, financial costs, income tax expense and profit allocation.',
    regnskapKontoplanWhatTitle: 'What is NS 4102?',
    regnskapKontoplanWhatBody: 'Norwegian Standard 4102 is the industry-standard chart of accounts in Norway — a common reference that allows financial statements from different companies to be compared. The SAF-T reporting to the Tax Authority is based on the same structure, and most accounting systems are delivered with NS 4102 as the starting point.',
    regnskapKontoplanHowTitle: 'How to choose the right account?',
    regnskapKontoplanHowBody: 'Find the class first. Assets are 1, liabilities and equity 2, and revenue 3. Costs sit in 4 (goods), 5 (payroll) and 6–7 (other operating costs). Financial items, tax and allocation of the profit for the year are 8. Then choose the two-digit group that fits best. Rent for premises, for example, is 63.',
    regnskapKontoplanDebKredTitle: 'Debit and credit',
    regnskapKontoplanDebKredBody: 'Every transaction is recorded with a debit on one account and a credit on another — the amounts must always be equal. This is called double-entry bookkeeping and is the fundamental rule that keeps the balance sheet in balance.',
    regnskapKontoplanCtaTitle: 'More accounting tools',
    regnskapKontoplanCtaBody: 'Set up an <a href="/regnskap/resultat/">income statement</a> and <a href="/regnskap/balanse/">balance sheet</a>, follow the <a href="/regnskap/kontantstrom/">cash flow</a>, work out the <a href="/regnskap/mva/">VAT return</a>, or learn bookkeeping with <a href="/regnskap/skatteavstemming/">tax reconciliation</a> and <a href="/regnskap/avsetninger/">provisions</a>.',
