    kalkMarginEx1Lbl: 'Shop · fixed margin',
    kalkMarginEx1Desc: 'Cost of goods 100 kr, target margin 40 %. Price = 100 / (1 − 0.40).',
    kalkMarginEx2Lbl: 'Online shop · markup',
    kalkMarginEx2Desc: 'Cost of goods 100 kr, markup 60 %. The margin becomes 37.5 %.',
    kalkMarginEx3Lbl: 'Known price · find the margin',
    kalkMarginEx3Desc: 'Price 249 kr, cost of goods 150 kr. Margin = 99 / 249.',
    kalkMarginFaqQ1: 'Are avanse and påslag the same thing?',
    kalkMarginFaqA1: 'Yes — both are calculated as a percentage of the cost of goods. “Avanse” is the retail-trade word, “påslag” the everyday one. Both are higher than the contribution margin ratio.',
    kalkMarginFaqQ2: 'Why is a 60 % markup only a 37.5 % margin?',
    kalkMarginFaqA2: 'The markup is calculated on the low cost of goods (100 kr), the margin on the higher selling price (160 kr). The same 60 kr, two denominators.',
    kalkMarginFaqQ3: 'Should VAT be part of the calculation?',
    kalkMarginFaqA3: 'No. Calculate margin and markup on prices excl. VAT. VAT is added to the selling price at the end and is collected on behalf of the state.',
    kalkMarginRel1Desc: 'How many units must you sell to cover the fixed costs?',
    kalkMarginRel2Desc: 'From the salary you want to what you actually have to invoice per hour.',
